seine (0.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make snapshot-pinned rootfs builds byte-reproducible: fixed
    container hostname, mmdebstrap timestamps taken from the spec
    mtime, dropped apt/ldconfig caches, truncated apt/dpkg logs,
    update-initramfs under SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, and an empty
    /etc/machine-id. Install ca-certificates before switching the
    host bootstrap, sbuild chroot or target rootfs to the pinned
    https feed.
  * Make disk image builds byte-reproducible: derive GPT and
    filesystem UUIDs from the spec digest, rebuild FAT/ext
    partitions with pinned serials, seeds and timestamps, and
    normalize fstab and grub hints. Pin LVM UUIDs (explicit
    --uuid, vgcfgbackup/vgcfgrestore with metadata scrub) under a
    frozen faketime clock.
  * Add resource-aware task concurrency to the scheduler: each task
    declares a cost against a resource class, configurable with
    '--resource CLASS=N', '/set resources' and the TUI Settings
    screen, with ageing of ready tasks so large jobs cannot starve.
  * Write logs/index.json after each run, flagging cache-hit tasks,
    and index test runs under logs/tests/index.json, so the TUI
    knows which logs belong to the open build.
  * Drive the TUI's right pane from the spec-tree selection, show
    loaded spec files with git status and lock marks on the root
    node, render disk layout as proportional boxes, and show
    relevant per-task log links on task-backed nodes.
  * Show test status in the overview pane with live refresh, list
    past runs with log and replay links, and replay a test's
    console recording in place (/replay, space to pause, left/right
    for speed, Esc to stop) with its keyword timeline and call
    arguments beside it.
  * Show package defects from UDD beside CVE findings on the
    /issues screen, as a per-source matrix with in-place entry
    lists.
  * Polish TUI behaviour: expand/collapse the spec tree with arrow
    keys, label bare list items with their only child's key, copy
    selected text to clipboard on mouse release, hide the empty
    packages barrier, remember the plan baseline after a build,
    refresh any screen when a build or test run progresses, hold
    the prompt shut while startup commands run, clip live progress
    lines to the terminal width, strip escape sequences from log
    panes, and drain the console stream before disconnecting so
    recordings keep their tail.
  * Rebuild pc-uki-image's kernel slim, sharing one config-fragment
    trim between the initrd and UKI groups, and drop the
    efibootguard variant from the minimal-uki example.

 -- Cedric Hombourger <chombourger@gmail.com>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:39:19 +0200

seine (0.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a 'seine podman' command, a dumb passthrough to podman pointed at
    seine's own storage.
  * Add squashfs/erofs support for read-only partitions and volumes: the
    imager stages and builds them itself, with no tooling needed on the
    target.
  * Add a 'multiconfig:' key to declare named sub-builds inside one
    specification file, each with its own packages and playbook.
  * Add 'source:' on partitions/volumes, routing a mount to a declared
    'multiconfig:' group's own root filesystem, for several
    independently-packaged operating systems on one disk.
  * Author one GRUB menu entry per 'multiconfig:' group sharing a disk,
    with a configurable boot-owner group.
  * Add an 'initrd:' output section to build and deploy a standalone
    initramfs artifact, without partitioning or an image.
  * Add 'extends: uki:' packaging, wrapping a kernel and deployed initrd
    into an installable Unified Kernel Image package (ukify or
    efibootguard backend).
  * Add a systemd-boot bootloader backend, booting Unified Kernel Images
    through the Boot Loader Specification's own auto-discovery.
  * Give root, /usr, /var, /var/tmp, /home and /srv partitions their own
    Discoverable Partition Specification GPT type, so a UKI can boot
    with root=/dev/gpt-auto.
  * Add 'multiconfig: after:'/'before:' ordering, chaining groups (e.g.
    initrd, then UKI, then rootfs) so one 'seine build' runs the whole
    pipeline.
  * Add dm-verity support for read-only partitions: pair a
    'verity: true' partition with a 'type: verity-hash' one, and the
    imager derives both partitions' GPT GUIDs from the built root hash.
  * Anchor a verity-protected UKI with 'usrhash=' once the root hash is
    known, and sign it with 'image: secure-boot:' if given.
  * Render each 'multiconfig:' group's own sub-build in the TUI's spec
    tree, and let /side-load and /side-unload target a named group.
  * Fix peer files (given on the command line or side-loaded) to amend
    an earlier file field by field instead of losing to it.

 -- Cedric Hombourger <chombourger@gmail.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 21:43:02 +0200

seine (0.1-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add seine-oci-<release>-<hostarch> packages: prebuilt bootstrap,
    vendor and sbuild OCI images and chroots under /usr/share/seine/oci,
    imported into podman automatically instead of being built from
    scratch.
  * Add i386 to the imager's per-architecture tables (kernel package,
    hypervisor, appliance triplet), next to the amd64/arm64/armhf
    entries already there.
  * Only fetch the qemu-user-static interpreter a HostBootstrap really
    needs to cross-bootstrap another architecture, instead of the whole
    qemu-user package (~465MiB for every architecture QEMU supports).
    amd64 and i386, or arm64 and armhf, need no interpreter at all: the
    CPU already runs that code natively.
  * Fix pybuild installing seine's own Python code into a directory
    dh_install never packaged (debian/python3-seine, guessed from
    PYBUILD_NAME): seine.deb shipped no code at all until now.
  * Make seine Architecture: amd64 arm64 instead of all, and bundle
    the 'ai', 'tui' and 'test' extras' pip-only deps (litellm, textual,
    robotframework, ...) under /usr/share/seine/pylibs: none of them
    have a Debian package, so a plain apt install used to leave those
    features needing a hand-built venv. seine-oci-<release>-<hostarch>
    packages are now only built on a native (non-cross) run.

 -- Cedric Hombourger <chombourger@gmail.com>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 07:28:59 +0200

